LA  - English
KW  - remote sensing; precision agriculture; artificial intelligence; soil moisture; vegetation indices
AB  - In today's agricultural landscape, precision is crucial, utilizing advanced technologies like IoT, AI, aircraft, and satellite systems. Smart agriculture aims to revolutionize production by monitoring soil quality and employing data anUAVs, remote sensing provides crucial data and imagery for olive cultivation. Cloud platforms with satellite data offer invaluable information, aiding public and private decision-making. Proposing an AI-powered application combined with remote sensing, this paper develops predictive models for soil moisture and with decision tree and extra trees regressor models, highlighting their effectiveness. This research transforms agricultural productivity through advanced technology and data-driven methodologies.
