AB  - As the global population continues to expand, the agriculture sector faces increasing pressure to produce more food while minimizing its environmental footprint. Energy use in farming plays a crucial role in achieving sustainable agricultural practices. This chapter explores various energy-efficient approaches in farming aimed at enhancing productivity, reducing costs, and mitigating environmental impacts. It examines key strategies such as precision agriculture, renewable energy integration, optimized machinery usage, and sustainable irrigation techniques. Precision agriculture utilizes advanced technologies such as GPS, drones, and sensors to optimize inputs such as water, fertilizers, and pesticides, thereby reducing energy consumption and minimizing environmental impacts. Integration of renewable energy sources such as solar, wind, and biomass offers opportunities to decarbonize farming operations while providing a reliable and cost-effective energy supply. Additionally, optimizing machinery usage through proper maintenance, sizing, and operation schedules can significantly reduce energy consumption and increase operational efficiency. Sustainable irrigation techniques, including drip irrigation and soil moisture monitoring, help minimize water and energy waste while maintaining crop productivity. This abstract discusses the economic, environmental, and social benefits of energy-efficient farming practices and highlights the importance of policy support and stakeholder engagement in their adoption and implementation. By embracing energy-efficient approaches, farmers can enhance their resilience to climate change, improve their competitiveness, and contribute to a more sustainable and resilient agricultural sector. © 2025 The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
