T2  - 2025 United States National Committee of URSI National Radio Science Meeting, USNC-URSI NRSM 2025 - Proceedings
LA  - English
KW  - Fertilizers; Global positioning system; Precision agriculture; Reflectometers; Soil surveys; Storms; Tropics; Agriculture industries; Fresh Water; Grid size; Precision Agriculture; Reflectometry; Size optimization; Soil moisture estimation; Soil moisture measurement; Sustainable practices; Water use; Soil moisture
AB  - The agriculture industry consumes 70% of the world's available freshwater, making efficient water use essential to ensuring sustainable practices. Precision agriculture, through accurate soil moisture (SM) measurements, can play a pivotal role in optimizing irrigation, reducing water wastage, and conserving critical resources. However, obtaining precise SM data across large agricultural areas remains a significant challenge. In-situ invasive SM probes can deliver highly accurate data but are limited to localized, point-based measurements that do not provide complete field coverage. Conversely, satellite-based SM measurements, such as those from the Cyclone Global Navigation Satellite System (CYGNSS), Soil Moisture Active Passive (SMAP), etc., offer extensive coverage but at resolutions (in kilometer range) that are insufficient for the high spatio-temporal accuracy required in precision agriculture. © 2025 USNC-URSI.
