AB  - This work presents a novel IoT-based multi-drone coordination strategy for precision agriculture, focusing on optimizing soil moisture monitoring. The proposed method leverages a centralized base station to dynamically assign tasks to drones, minimizing redundant measurements while ensuring critical areas are prioritized. By integrating penalties based on estimated soil moisture levels and flight time, the approach balances mission time and efficiency. Experimental validation using simulated soil moisture maps demonstrates robust performance across various initial configurations, achieving high success rates and efficient exploration. The results highlight the adaptability of the method to diverse scenarios, with potential applications in wildfire risk assessment, environmental monitoring, and infrastructure inspection.  © 2025 IEEE.
