AU  - Nivethitha, T.; Deebanchakkarawarthi, G.; Kavitha, N.
TI  - Cultivating Tomorrow: The Synergy of AI and IoT in Agriculture
T2  - AIoT: Artificial Intelligence of Things
LA  - English
KW  - Agricultural robots; Crop protection; Dairy products; Fumigation; Harvesters; Insect control; Orchards; Precision agriculture; Seed; Vegetables; Weed control; Agriculture industries; Climate prediction; Crop monitoring; Intelligent irrigations; Irrigation crops; Precision-farming; Resources optimization; Soil moisture sensors; Supply chain optimization; Weather patterns; Irrigation
AB  - AIoT—the fusion of Artificial Intelligence (AI) with the Internet of Things (IoT)—has the potential to completely transform the agriculture industry. The increasing problems that farmers are facing—from precision farming to resource optimization—are addressed by this synergy. This means that AIoT uses in agriculture include a wide range of topics, such as climate prediction, supply chain optimization, intelligent irrigation, crop monitoring, animal management, and autonomous farming equipment. By utilizing IoT devices, including drones and soil moisture sensors, to gather data in real time on crop health, weather patterns, and soil conditions, AIoT facilitates precision farming. After analyzing this data, AI systems provide farmers with the information they need to decide when to sow, water, and fertilize. By optimizing water usage, cutting waste, and boosting efficiency, smart irrigation systems are made possible by IoT sensors and AI analytics. Utilizing drones, wearable sensors, and satellite imaging, AIoT improves crop and livestock monitoring. Farmers can benefit from early diagnosis and preventive steps by using AI-driven analytics, which offers useful information on crop health, potential diseases, and livestock behavior. Radio Frequency Identification (RFID) technology and AI analytics are utilized to enhance the agricultural supply chain, resulting in improved logistics, decreased waste, and better product flow. AI-driven navigation on autonomous farming equipment helps to boost productivity in operations like planting, harvesting, and pest management. Furthermore, AIoT contributes to climate change prediction by analyzing historical weather data and generating accurate forecasts that let farmers adjust their activities in response to changing weather patterns. In conclusion, the application of AIoT in agriculture signifies a radical shift in perspective. By leveraging AI and IoT, farmers may achieve data-driven, efficient, and sustainable farming techniques that will ultimately improve environmental sustainability and global food security. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Arun Sekar Rajasekaran, Fadi Al-Turjman, and Suganyadevi S; individual chapters, the contributors.
