TI  - Maximizing Wheat Crop Productivity with Intelligent Land Analysis and IoT
T2  - 2024 International Conference on Recent Innovation in Smart and Sustainable Technology, ICRISST 2024
LA  - English
KW  - Agricultural Productivity; Crop Health Monitoring; Data Analytics; Internet of Things (IoT); Machine Learning; Soil Sensors; Wheat Crop; % reductions; Agricultural productivity; Crop health monitoring; Crop productivity; Data analytics; Health monitoring; Internet of thing; Machine-learning; Soil sensors; Wheat crop; Smart agriculture
AB  - Agricultural productivity plays an essential role in global food security, with a special focus on increasing the production of important crops such as wheat. To meet the requirement, the study proposes a novel technique that combines an intelligent land analysis framework with IoT (Internet of Things) technology. The growing global population and the limitations of traditional farming methods in meeting expanding demand create a pressing requirement for such a model. Existing methods tend to be limited by a lack of real-time data, resulting in inefficient resource usage and yield losses. The proposed method, on the other hand, merges soil sensors, drones, and satellite images to provide farmers with real-time information on soil moisture, levels of nutrients, and the health of crops. It employs data analytics and machine learning algorithms to provide personalized irrigation, fertilization, and pest control recommendations, allowing for accurate and timely interventions. Field experiments reveal a 20% increase in wheat yield, 15% reduction in water use and 18% reduction in fertilizer usage, demonstrating the effectiveness of the method compared with the existing approach in increasing productivity while saving resources and avoiding environmental impacts. © 2024 IEEE.
