AB  - The Canopy Geometric Structure for Crop Yield Estimation Using PCA-Driven Machine Learning Models with Hyperspectral Images (CGCPMH) utilizes UAV-mounted hyperspectral imagery for estimating plant biomass and evaluating vegetation. The approach involves a preprocessing pipeline that improves image quality and segmentation through CIELAB color space transformation. Principal Component Analysis (PCA) facilitates data dimensionality reduction, enabling extraction of key spectral features relevant to soil moisture. Precision canopy monitoring is accomplished through voxel-based 3D modeling. This methodology supports decision-making in precision agriculture, providing a framework for sustainable practices in Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs). The following specifications spike weight and plant height analysis, gain weight analysis, error estimation, RMSE, and MAE calculations. © 2025 IEEE.
