AU  - Belinda, C.M.; Kannan, E.; Sivagami, S.; James, J.W.
TI  - Enhancing precision farming through IoT: Advanced sensor applications and data strategies in agriculture
T2  - AIoT and Smart Sensing: A Comprehensive Guide to the Next Generation of Smart Devices
LA  - English
AB  - This work provides a comprehensive examination of precision farming, an innovative agricultural approach leveraging technology to enhance practices, boost crop yields, and mitigate environmental impacts. It underscores the importance of addressing challenges posed by a growing global population and changing environmental conditions. The role of the Internet of Things (IoT) in facilitating data gathering and informed decision-making is highlighted, particularly through sensors and data collection techniques. Various technologies such as weather stations, drones, remote sensing satellites, and IoT soil moisture sensors are explored for their contributions to large-scale farm management, crop monitoring, and irrigation optimisation. The mechanisms for data collection, transmission, integration, and processing are thoroughly investigated, along with security considerations in IoT systems for agriculture. The work includes instructive case studies illustrating the transformative potential of precision farming in areas like satellite-based agriculture, drone-based crop monitoring, and smart irrigation systems. Real-life examples demonstrate the benefits of precision farming in resource conservation, crop quality improvement, and environmental sustainability worldwide. Precision farming utilises IoT technology such as wireless sensor networks, remote sensing, GPS, variable rate technology, farm management systems, smart irrigation, and artificial intelligence to promote sustainable agriculture. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Vaishali R. Kulkarni, Thompson Stephan, Punitha S, Fadi Al-Turjman and Thinagaran Perumal.
