KW  - AeroAgriNet; Agricultural IoT; Distributed AI; Edge Intelligence; Flying Edge Computing; Precision Farming; Real-Time Analytics; Smart Agriculture; Swarm UAVs; Aircraft detection; Antennas; Cloud analytics; Edge computing; Flight dynamics; Internet of things; Precision agriculture; Smart agriculture; Swarm intelligence; Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAV); Aerial vehicle; Aeroagrinet; Agricultural IoT; Distributed AI; Edge computing; Edge intelligence; Flying edge computing; Precision-farming; Real-time analytics; Smart agricultures; Swarm unmanned aerial vehicle; Decision making
AB  - Existing agricultural practices encounter several challenges, including worker scarcity intermixed with climate volatility and mounting pressure for sustainable operations. These agricultural issues need innovative solutions integrating real time capabilities with intelligence and mobile control and scalability aspects. The paper conceptualizes AeroAgriNet as a swarm-enabled flying edge architecture constructed with Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) to provide real-time agricultural intelligence. As a distributed smart aerial edge network, the AeroAgriNet swarm continuously carries out real-time processing of agro-environmental input while offering sensing and responsive capabilities. The envisioned system merges edge computing with AI-driven data analytics and dynamic UAV coordination to undertake crucial agricultural activities such as crop health monitoring and soil moisture analysis and pest detection. AeroAgriNet leverages a multi-layered infrastructure of edge AI processors, utilizing smart UAV swarms and cloud analytics platforms to enable latency-aware operational decisions and scalable deployment. The assessment demonstrates impressive performance gains for data collection speed and accurate decision-making and monitoring area coverage over conventional UAV observation practices.  © 2025 IEEE.
