AB  - We are all aware of how agriculture has become gambling. Weather, water scarcity, soil fertility, pesticides are the key role players in it. To strengthen the quality and quantity of the agriculture production, the farmer of 21st century needs to access the smart farming solutions, which enable them to Sense for soil moisture and nutrients, to collect data and to analyze every minute inch of crop and its growth, to report weather forecast etc. Such smart farming solution is the Internet of Things (IoT) based Agriculture or IoT-enabled smart farming. The world of IoT is expanding across the world making things smarter resulting in bigger and qualitative productivity. In addition, in agriculture, the IoT has brought the greatest impact. IoT-enabled smart farming has come up as a special wave in agriculture. Smart farming is key for the future of agriculture. IoT will make agriculture industry beneficiary. The farmers are getting twofold benefits by adopting IoT. With accurate data, it has helped farmers to reduce their costs and improve yield growth at the same time. Few applications of IoT in agriculture includes automatic water sprinkling, precision agriculture, remote crop monitoring, climate monitoring and forecasting, better water management possible when coupled with sensors, data and other machinery etc. In this chapter, we will explore the components of smart farming, framing sensors, farming drones, IoT network, network and data protocols and use cases of IoT in farming and challenges in IoT-based farming. © 2021 Nova Science Publishers, Inc.
