AU  - Pawan, Y.V.R.N.; Prakash, K.B.
TI  - Enhancing Connectivity and Data-Driven Decision-Making for Smart Agriculture by Embracing 6G Technology
T2  - Development of 6G Networks and Technology
LA  - English
KW  - 6G technology; artificial intelligence; data-driven decision-making; edge computing; enhanced connectivity; precision agriculture; predictive analytics; smart agriculture
AB  - This book chapter scrupulously analyzes the prospective utilization of 6G technology for smart agriculture. This chapter emphasizes improved connection and data-driven decision-making. It focuses on the need for in-time data analysis and effective communication in advancing sustainable farming practices. This chapter also summarizes the anticipated 6G characteristics, like extensive machine communications, ultra-reliable and low-latency connections, high-speed data transmission, edge computing, and integration of AI. A number of 6G smart agricultural applications, such as precision agriculture, which looks at the current crop health, soil moisture, and weather data to determine the most efficient resource management and distribution methods, are examined in this chapter. The deployment of state-of-the-art technology and better-quality photographs also illustrates how 6G networks can monitor agriculture rapidly and efficiently. The focus of investigations into edge computing and AI algorithms is on their ability to make real-time decisions based on data gathered by sensors, drones, or other devices. Furthermore, this chapter provides an overview of how 6G will allow robotics and autonomous systems to work in synergy and carry out specific tasks according to the evolving landscape of agriculture. The benefits of better monitoring and predictive analysis are also highlighted in this chapter. Farmers may use 6G to deploy sensors and the Internet of Things (IoT) devices to obtain real-time weather data, the current state of the soil, quality of crops, or animal activity. Forecasts for weather trends, disease outbreaks, and crop yields will be made using predictive analytic techniques based on AI and advanced data analysis. The chapter briefs the features and challenges when adopting 6G for smart agriculture, such as addressing infrastructure, privacy and security issues, and interdisciplinary cooperation. Comprehensively, this book chapter highlights the profound potential of 6G technology in smart agriculture, which offers improved connection and data utilization to promote production, sustainability, and efficiency. © 2025 Scrivener Publishing LLC. All rights reserved.
