KW  - Antennas; Climate change; Crops; Information management; Soil moisture; Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAV); Aerial vehicle; Agricultural sector; Body potential; Changing needs; Economic development; Food manufacturers; Governing bodies; Human survival; Primary sources; Well being; Farms
AB  - Agriculture plays a pivotal role in fostering economic development and well-being. It holds immense significance for human survival as it serves as a primary source of sustenance. In order to meet the ever-changing needs of our planet, farmers are tasked with meeting the evolving demands stipulated by governing bodies, potential consumers, food manufacturers, and sellers. However, the agricultural sector faces mounting challenges such as climate change, soil degradation, plant diseases, and other factors, which exert increasing pressure on the growth and productivity of crops. Drone refers to an unmanned aerial vehicle specifically designed for use in agricultural activities. The "Sky Farm UAV for Agriculture" is a cutting-edge final year project that focuses on the development ofan advanced unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) tailored for precision agriculture. The primary objective of this project is to design and implement a versatile UAV platform equipped with sophisticated sensors capable of detecting critical agriculturalparameters such as temperature, soil moisture, and disease presence. Leveraging state-of-the-art technology, the Sky Farm UAV aims to empower farmers with real-time, high-resolution data to optimize crop management practices, enhance resource efficiency, and improve overall agricultural productivity. © 2023 IEEE.
