AB  - The article is devoted to the study of the use of neural networks to improve the selection of plant stands in precision agriculture technologies. The study takes into account the complex aspects of sample selection, such as the speed of image acquisition, the effectiveness of assessing the state of mineral nutrition and soil moisture, etc. The use of neural networks makes it possible to automate and increase the accuracy of selection, improving the quality of the analysis of plant stands, subject to compliance with soil sample evaluation technologies. The obtained results indicate the prospects of implementing this approach in modern agriculture. © 2023 Copyright for this paper by its authors.
