T2  - 2024 1st International Conference on Sustainability and Technological Advancements in Engineering Domain, SUSTAINED 2024
LA  - English
KW  - Agricultural Technology; Crop Management; Data Analytics in Agriculture; Predictive Analytics; Soil Health Monitoring; Sustainable Farming; Agricultural machinery; Agricultural technology; Crops; Decision making; Information management; Internet of things; Learning algorithms; Learning systems; Machine learning; Natural resources management; Precision agriculture; Smart agriculture; Agricultural technologies; Crop managements; Data analytic in agriculture; Data analytics; Health monitoring; Machine-learning; Precision Agriculture; Soil health; Soil health monitoring; Sustainable Farming; Predictive analytics
AB  - The combination of technology that is connected to the Internet of Things (IoT) and Machine Learning (ML) has resulted in a revolution in precision agriculture, which has made it possible for advancements to be made in agricultural operations that are more intelligent. The purpose of this study is to investigate the ways in which machine learning (ML) and the Internet of Things (IoT) could work together to improve crop yields, resource management, and agricultural operations. A complete picture of agricultural dynamics can be painted with the assistance of Internet of Things (IoT) technology such as sensors and drones, with the latter being one example. Real-time information regarding the soil, the weather, and the health of the crop is provided by these devices. It is possible for machine learning algorithms to sift through vast amounts of data, recognize patterns, and then automate decision-making based on the results of their analysis. The research investigates a number of critical areas where machine learning and the Internet of Things combine, including the regulation of soil moisture, the detection of pests and diseases, and the forecasting of agricultural yields. These are the issues that are subjected to the investigation. It is possible for farmers to achieve more exact irrigation scheduling, faster pest management interventions, and accurate yield projections by utilizing data collecting that is enabled by the IoT and predictive models that are developed from ML. By using this technique, not only is operational expense reduced, but environmental effect is reduced as well. On top of that, the research contains case studies that show how these technologies have been used in real-life farming situations. Significant improvements in resource utilization, operational efficiency, and total agricultural productivity were shown by the outcomes of these case studies. Concerns about data security, integration challenges, and financial ramifications are just a few of the challenges that the paper identifies as being associated with using IoT and ML technologies. To sum up, precision agriculture's utilization of AI and the IoT brings several notable benefits, including better management of resources, higher crop yields, and more efficient farming. In order to tackle new challenges and drive smart farming into the future, this study's conclusions stress the importance of investing in and maintaining innovation.  © 2024 IEEE.
