AB  - Advances in 3D printing have brought that technology into the smooth and easy creation of extremely complex shapes. The paper, therefore, presents a complete overview of the various possibilities of the practical implementation of 3D printing for the purposes of precision agriculture. Developed, through that technology, is a housing for the soil moisture sensor system. The sensor underwent rigorous testing for a period of three months and demonstrated excellent operational performance, with the material from which it is made exhibiting great strength and resilience to the variability in the specific agro-climatic conditions. Built, additionally, was a stand capable of accommodating four multispectral drone cameras. Achieved, as a result, was optimal strength with minimum weight in view of the specific volume to be filled up. The technology, hereto described, shows great promise as an environmentally friendly approach to the construction of intricate shapes.  © 2023 IEEE.
